<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul stocks closed for National Holiday.</title>
<headline>Seoul stocks closed for National Holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Korean stock market was closed on Friday for Memorial Day and will reopen on Saturday, brokers said.</p>
<p>The composite stock index closed on Thursday 2.42 points higher at 765.67 on foreign buying of electricity-monopoly KEPCO and some securities houses.</p>
<p>Brokers said falling interest rates also helped boost investors' sentiment.</p>
<p>-- Yeom Yoon-jeong (822) 727 5647</p>
